From 1e02b8bcbe2b1f0fd7d16d33ea4b1b2a5c325dc8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:25:58 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mask): keep original frames when no mouth is visible
 instead of stopping or mosaicking

Frames without landmarks used to stop strict clothing exports or paint a face mosaic,
even when the mouth was above the frame edge or the head was turned away. A current-frame
check (face-skin segmentation + lip parsing) now keeps those frames untouched; visible but
untracked lips, or any check failure, still use the existing guard.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015XEHdEnhr7p5ae4FL4TjbE
